          "topic": "Newton's second law and momentum",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Newton's second law relates the net force on an object to the rate of change of its momentum. For constant mass, the familiar form is F_net = m a. Acceleration points in the direction of the net force; forces from different interactions must be added as vectors before applying the law.",
