          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Motion in a Plane",
          "topic": "Projectile motion",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Ideal projectile motion separates into horizontal and vertical components. Neglecting air resistance, horizontal acceleration is zero and vertical acceleration is -g when upward is positive. The two components share the same time; this lets us combine horizontal uniform motion with vertical accelerated motion.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-physics-11",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-physics-042",
