          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Motion in a Plane",
          "topic": "Projectile motion",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "A ball is launched horizontally at 10 m/s from a 20 m high ledge. With g = 10 m/s^2, the fall time satisfies 20 = (1/2)gt^2, so t = 2 s. The horizontal range is 10 × 2 = 20 m.",
