          "subject": "Physics",
          "class": 11,
          "chapter": "Laws of Motion",
          "topic": "Static and kinetic friction",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "A 10 kg box rests on a level floor with μ_s = 0.4 and g = 10 m/s². The normal force is 100 N, so maximum static friction is 40 N. A 25 N horizontal pull can be balanced by 25 N of static friction, and the box stays still.",
          "reference_id": "adapted-original-physics-11",
          "syllabus_reference_id": "cbse-2026-27-physics-042",
          "page_start": null,
          "page_end": null,
          "language": "en",
          "review_status": "teacher_review_required"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "phy11-friction-misconception-001",
