          "chapter": "Gravitation",
          "topic": "Universal gravitation and gravitational field",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Any two masses attract with force F = Gm₁m₂/r² along the line joining their centres. The gravitational field strength is force per unit test mass. For a spherical body outside it, the field behaves as if the mass were concentrated at its centre.",
